  "query_preview": "/SUNDAY NIGHT THROUGH THURSDAY/...\nIssued at 212 PM CDT Fri Jul 31 2026\n\nMonday...Highs to range in the 90s, with near 100 possible across \nsouthwest NE. NBM probabilities of 100 degrees or warmer are from 30 \nto near 60 percent across southwest Nebraska. The upper ridge will \nbreak down across the Northern Plains as an upper trough moves into \nMontana. This will bring a cold front across northeast Wyoming and \nwestern South Dakota into northwest Nebraska. Another day of \nincreased fire weather concerns, especially west of Highway 83. \nDetails can be found in the Fire Weather section below. \n\nA cold front is forecast to move through the forecast area Monday \nnight and stall out across northern Kansas through Wednesday night. \nThis will bring increased chances for showers and thunderstorms \nMonday night through Wednesday night. This also bring a cooldown \nwith highs Tuesday only in the mid 70s north central to low 80s \nsouthwest, with upper 70s to mid 80s Wednesday. \n\nThursday into Friday...Looks mainly dry with highs by Friday with \nhighs returning to the 90s.",
